{
  "dom_id": "step-q37893",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+5x-3 \\\\  & 5x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{10{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,25{x}^{2}-10x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{25{x}^{2}+5x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-15x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,15x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3}{5x+1}=$",
  "worked_solution": "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+5x-3 \\\\  & 5x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{10{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,25{x}^{2}-10x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{25{x}^{2}+5x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-15x-3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,15x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3$ by the linear binomial $5x+1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $2{x}^{2}+5x-3,$ and\n\n- the remainder $0.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{10{x}^{3}+27{x}^{2}-10x-3}{5x+1}=2{x}^{2}+5x-3+\\frac{0}{5x+1}=2{x}^{2}+5x-3.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
